<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Albert, King of Sweden</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1338–<a href="/years/1412">1412</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> · Also known as Albert of Sweden</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Albert, King of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a>, also known as Albert of Mecklenburg, reigned from 1364 to 1389, after Swedish nobles deposed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/magnus-eriksson">Magnus Eriksson</a> and offered him the crown. His reliance on German advisers made him unpopular, and the nobles turned to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/margaret-i-of-denmark">Margaret I of Denmark</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norway">Norway</a>, whose forces defeated and captured him at Åsle in 1389. Released in 1395, he later ruled as Duke of Mecklenburg.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/albert-king-of-sweden.jpg" alt="Albert, King of Sweden" width="320" height="423" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jacob Truedson Demitz for Ristesson. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Albert_of_Sweden_effigy_2010.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
